A sensor board should still sense the

2
00:00:01,725 --> 00:00:02,866
world after you put it in a

3
00:00:02,866 --> 00:00:03,547
case.

4
00:00:04,225 --> 00:00:06,688
This Arduino Nano thirty-three B L E

5
00:00:06,688 --> 00:00:08,861
Sense revision two enclosure is designed with

6
00:00:08,861 --> 00:00:12,198
OpenAI Codex, in real FreeCAD, recorded with

7
00:00:12,198 --> 00:00:13,086
OBS.

8
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:16,346
Arduino supplies the mechanical drawing.

9
00:00:17,023 --> 00:00:19,074
The board is forty-three point one six

10
00:00:19,074 --> 00:00:21,576
by seventeen point seven six millimetres.

11
00:00:22,254 --> 00:00:24,171
Four mounting holes are one point six

12
00:00:24,171 --> 00:00:26,526
five millimetres across, on a forty point

13
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,358
six four by fifteen point two four

14
00:00:28,358 --> 00:00:28,870
grid.

15
00:00:29,798 --> 00:00:31,994
We turn those dimensions into a rounded

16
00:00:31,994 --> 00:00:33,984
shell with two point four millimetre walls

17
00:00:33,984 --> 00:00:34,727
and floor.

18
00:00:35,404 --> 00:00:37,504
The dimensions remain editable in the native

19
00:00:37,504 --> 00:00:38,234
document.

20
00:00:38,912 --> 00:00:40,586
This is a design you can adjust,

21
00:00:40,586 --> 00:00:41,705
not just a picture.

22
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:44,295
Four supports locate the board at its

23
00:00:44,295 --> 00:00:45,438
mounting holes.

24
00:00:46,116 --> 00:00:48,278
Separate posts hold the removable lid.

25
00:00:48,955 --> 00:00:50,946
Board thickness is a provisional one point

26
00:00:50,946 --> 00:00:51,967
six millimetres;

27
00:00:51,989 --> 00:00:54,271
screw choice and component clearance still need

28
00:00:54,271 --> 00:00:54,892
checking.

29
00:00:55,819 --> 00:00:58,601
A micro USB opening faces the connector.

30
00:00:59,278 --> 00:01:01,538
Long slots keep the pin headers accessible.

31
00:01:02,215 --> 00:01:04,157
The broad centre opening gives the sensors

32
00:01:04,157 --> 00:01:05,700
access to air and light.

33
00:01:06,378 --> 00:01:08,671
The finished enclosure still needs real sensing

34
00:01:08,671 --> 00:01:10,045
and wireless tests.

35
00:01:10,972 --> 00:01:12,392
Lift the lid and see the board

36
00:01:12,392 --> 00:01:13,584
seated inside.

37
00:01:14,261 --> 00:01:16,652
We use Arduino's official board artwork as

38
00:01:16,652 --> 00:01:18,183
a flat visual reference.

39
00:01:18,861 --> 00:01:20,535
It shows the layout, but does not

40
00:01:20,535 --> 00:01:22,589
prove component heights or clearance.

41
00:01:23,266 --> 00:01:26,144
Only the enclosure is exported for manufacturing.

42
00:01:27,072 --> 00:01:28,953
The case parts are valid solids, with

43
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:31,492
